            %h2#11DSugraFromSuperCFieldFluxQuantization 11d-SuGra from Super C-Field Flux Quantization
            %p
              We discuss (Thm.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#11dSuGraEOMFromSuperFluxIdentity"}
              below, following
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "D=11+supergravity#GiotopoulosSatiSchreiber24"} GSS24, §3
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"} D=11 supergravity
              — on an
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 11
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 32
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 11\vert\mathbf{32}
              = succeed "-free" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-torsion"} super-torsion
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetime"} super spacetime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vielbein"} super vielbein
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi e
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e,\psi)
              (the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graviton"} graviton
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality-symmetric+higher+gauge+theory"} duality-symmetric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form+on+a+supermanifold"} super-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} C-field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+densities"} flux densities
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                        %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi G
                        %mn 7
                        %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi dR
                        %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi dR
                        %mn 7
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G_4^s, G_7^s) \,\in\, \Omega^4_{dR}(X) \times \Omega^7_{dR}(X)
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  satisfy their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identities"} Bianchi identities
                #eq:SuperFluxBianchiIdentity.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %msubsup
                                %mi G
                                %mn 4
                                %mi s
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mo =
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %msubsup
                                %mi G
                                %mn 7
                                %mi s
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mo =
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mfrac
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mn 2
                              %msubsup
                                %mi G
                                %mn 4
                                %mi s
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %msubsup
                                %mi G
                                %mn 4
                                %mi s
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\begin{array}{l}
                        \\mathrm{d} \, G_4^s \;=\; 0
                        \\\
                        \\mathrm{d} \, G_7^s \;=\; \tfrac{1}{2} G_4^s \, G_4^s
                        \\end{array}
              %li
                %p
                  are on any super-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chart"} chart
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \hookrightarrow X
                  of the locally supersymmetric form
                #eq:LocalFormOfSuperFluxDensities.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mi G
                                %mn 4
                                %mi s
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mo =
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mfrac
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mrow
                                    %mn 4
                                    %mo !
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi G
                                %mn 4
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mi ⋯
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 4
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 1
                              %mi ⋯
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 4
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo −
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mfrac
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mn 2
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                              %mover
                                %mi ψ
                                %mo ¯
                              %msub
                                %mi Γ
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 1
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 2
                              %mi ψ
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 1
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msubsup
                                %mi G
                                %mn 7
                                %mi s
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mo =
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mfrac
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mrow
                                    %mn 7
                                    %mo !
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi G
                                %mn 7
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mi ⋯
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 7
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 1
                              %mi ⋯
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 7
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo −
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mfrac
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mrow
                                    %mn 5
                                    %mo !
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                              %mover
                                %mi ψ
                                %mo ¯
                              %msub
                                %mi Γ
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mi ⋯
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 5
                              %mi ψ
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 1
                              %mi ⋯
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi a
                                    %mn 5
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\begin{array}{l}
                        G_4^s
                        \\;=\;
                        \\tfrac{1}{4!}
                        (G_4)_{a_1 \cdots a_4}
                        e^{a_1} \cdots e^{a_4}
                        \\,-\,
                        \\tfrac{1}{2}
                        \\big(\overline{\psi}\Gamma_{a_1 a_2} \psi\big)
                        e^{a_1} \, e^{a_2}
                        \\\
                        G_7^s
                        \\;=\;
                        \\tfrac{1}{7!}
                        (G_7)_{a_1 \cdots a_7}
                        e^{a_1} \cdots e^{a_7}
                        \\,-\,
                        \\tfrac{1}{5!}
                        \\big(\overline{\psi}\Gamma_{a_1 \cdots a_5} \psi\big)
                        e^{a_1} \cdots e^{a_5}
                        \\mathrlap{\,.}
                        \\end{array}
            %p
              Up to some mild (but suggestive, see below) re-arrangement, the computation is essentially that indicated in
              %a{:href => "D'Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity#CastellaniDAuriaFre"} CDF91, §III.8.5
              (where some of the easy checks are indicated) which in turn is a mild reformulation of the original claim in
              %a{:href => "#D=11+supergravity#CremmerFerrara80"} Cremmer &amp; Ferrara 1980
              and
              %a{:href => "D=11+supergravity#BrinkHowe80"} Brink &amp; Howe 1980
              (where less details were given). A full proof is laid out in
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "D=11+supergravity#GiotopoulosSatiSchreiber24"} GSS24, §3
            %p
              The following may be understood as an exposition of this result, which seems to stand out as the only account that is (i) fully
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+formulation+of+gravity"} first-order
              and (ii)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality-symmetric+higher+gauge+theory"} duality-symmetric
              (in that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_7
              enters the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation+of+motion"} EoMs
              as an independent field, whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+duality"} Hodge duality
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
              is imposed
              %em
                by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identity"} Bianchi identity
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi G
                        %mn 7
                        %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_7^s
            %p
              Notice that the discussion in
              %a{:href => "D'Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity#CastellaniDAuriaFre"} CDF91, §III.8
              amplifies the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
              %a{:href => "D'Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity#Rheonomy"} rheonomy principle
              as a constraint that makes the Bianchi identities on (in our paraphrase) a
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+6-algebra"} supergravity Lie 6-algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra+valued+differential+form"} valued
              higher vielbein be equivalent to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+SuGra"} D=11 SuGra
              %em constraint
              necessary is that
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LocalFormOfSuperFluxDensities"} (2)
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} C-field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
              — and this is the one not strictly given by rules in
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "D'Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity#CastellaniDAuriaFre"} CDF91, p. 874
              %a{:href => "D'Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity#CastellaniDAuriaFre"} CDF91, (III.8.41)
              —; while the remaining rheonomy condition on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              is
              %em implied
              (Lem.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperBianchiIdentityOnG4InComponents"}
              below), and the
              %a{:href => "torsion+constraints+in+supergravity#Examples11dSuGra"} all-important
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+constraints+in+supergravity"} torsion constraint
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TorsionConstraint"} (3)
              (which is also outside the rules of rheonomy constraints, cf.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "D'Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity#CastellaniDAuriaFre"} CDF91, (III.8.33)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-spacetime"} super-spacetime
              in the first place (Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperSpacetime"}
              below).
            %p In thus recasting the formulation of the theorem somewhat, we also:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  re-define the super-flux densities as above
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LocalFormOfSuperFluxDensities"} (2)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identity"} Bianchi identity
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SuperFluxBianchiIdentity"} (1)
                  extends to
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
              %li
                %p
                  disregard the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+potentials"} gauge potentials
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 3
